<Base title="About — ResearchVault">
  <div class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span>About</div>
  <h1>About this vault</h1>
  <p class="lede">A personal, evolving research library built to drill from sector theses down to individual company analysis.</p>

  <p>ResearchVault is a structured knowledge base. Each <strong>sector</strong> carries a top-level investment thesis; each <strong>sub-sector</strong> breaks the sector into segments with distinct economics; and each <strong>company</strong> is a deep-dive tagged back to its sector and sub-sector. The site is generated from Markdown — adding a new company is one file.</p>

  <h2>How it's organized</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Sectors</strong> — the big themes and the argument for why they matter now.</li>
    <li><strong>Sub-sectors</strong> — segments within a sector that behave differently (margins, moats, dynamics).</li>
    <li><strong>Companies</strong> — specific names, key facts, the thesis they express, and what to diligence.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="callout risk">
    <div class="h">Important Disclaimer</div>
    <p>This site is an independent analytical exercise for discussion and educational purposes only. It is not investment advice, a recommendation, or a solicitation to buy or sell any security, and it is not legal, tax, or financial advice. All figures are drawn from publicly available secondary sources, are time-sensitive, and may be inaccurate, incomplete, or superseded. Conduct independent due diligence and consult qualified professional advisers before making any decision.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
